# Two guests grab one guest's throw in flight at once. The first claim the host takes is a catch;
# the second finds the box already in a guest's hold and is refused, since only a flight is caught:
# no ping-pong. Every endpoint shows the box in the winner's hand, and the loser's copy goes to it.
scenario catch_race
scene four_chars_item
seed 41
guests 3
settle 6s

net g1 rtt 100ms jitter 10ms loss 1%
net g2 rtt 100ms jitter 10ms loss 1%
net g3 rtt 120ms jitter 10ms loss 1%

p1 grab box as lift
p1 wait 300ms
p1 throw 4 0.2 0 speed 9 as throw
p2 walk box speed 1 on throw as reach2
p2 grab box as c2
p2 wait 1500ms
p2 drop as put2
p3 walk box speed 1 on throw as reach3
p3 grab box as c3
p3 wait 1500ms
p3 drop as put3

expect result lift granted
expect result throw done
expect one_of granted c2 c3
expect one_of refused c2 c3
# No endpoint but the loser's own shows the box in her hand: the host never moved it to her.
expect held box p2 p3
expect agree_at_rest 5cm
expect no_stuck
expect late_drops.count >= 1
expect late_drops.count <= 30
expect local_correction.max <= 1cm
expect takes.count <= 0
expect reclaims.count <= 0
